.TH ORO-SEMVER 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:semver \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:semver'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
A SemVer 2.0.0 implementation backed by the native runtime. This module provides helpers for parsing, comparing, incrementing, and checking ranges.
.PP
Example: import * as semver from 'oro:semver'
.PP
const v = semver.parse('1.2.3\-alpha.1') if (!v) throw new Error('invalid') console.log(v.major, v.minor, v.patch, v.prerelease)
.PP
if (semver.satisfies('1.2.3', '>=1.0.0 <2.0.0')) { console.log('compatible') }
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBparse(version)\fR
Parse a semantic version string into its structured representation. Returns `null` when the input is not a valid SemVer 2.0.0 version.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIversion\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fISemVer \\| null\fR
.TP
\fBvalid(version)\fR
Returns the canonical version string when `version` is valid, otherwise `null`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIversion\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring \\| null\fR
.TP
\fBcompare(a, b)\fR
Compare two semantic versions.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIa\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIb\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fI\-1 \\| 0 \\| 1\fR
.TP
