\fBsatisfies(version, range)\fR
Test whether a version satisfies a range expression.
.br
Supported range grammar includes: \- Simple comparators (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, `=`, or bare versions) \- Hyphen ranges: `1.2.3 \- 2.3.4` \- Wildcard ranges: `1.x`, `1.2.x`, `1`, `1.2`, `*` \- Tilde ranges: `~1.2.3`, `~1.2`, `~1` \- Caret ranges: `^1.2.3`, `^0.2.3`, `^0.0.3` \- `||` for OR between sets of comparators
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIversion\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIrange\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIboolean\fR
.TP
\fBinc(version, release, preid)\fR
Increment a version according to the given release type.
.br
Release types: \- 'major', 'minor', 'patch' \- 'premajor', 'preminor', 'prepatch', 'prerelease'
.br
When a pre* release type is used, `preid` (when provided) becomes the pre\-release identifier (e.g., `beta` \-> `1.2.3\-beta.0`). If omitted, `rc` is used by default.
.br
Returns `null` when the input version is invalid.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIversion\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIrelease\fR (\&'major' \\| 'minor' \\| 'patch' \\| 'premajor' \\| 'preminor' \\| 'prepatch' \\| 'prerelease'; required)
.br
\fIpreid\fR (string; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring \\| null\fR
.TP
\fBclean(version)\fR
Clean a version by returning its canonical form or `null` when invalid.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIversion\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring \\| null\fR
.TP
\fBmajor(version)\fR
Extract the major component of a version or `NaN` when invalid.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIversion\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fInumber\fR
.TP
\fBminor(version)\fR
Extract the minor component of a version or `NaN` when invalid.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIversion\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fInumber\fR
.TP
\fBpatch(version)\fR
Extract the patch component of a version or `NaN` when invalid.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIversion\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fInumber\fR
.TP
\fBprerelease(version)\fR
Returns the prerelease components of a version or `null` when invalid or when the version has no prerelease identifiers.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIversion\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring[] \\| null\fR
.TP
\fBvalidRange(range)\fR
Validate and normalize a range expression. Returns the normalized comparator\-based range or `null` when invalid.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIrange\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring \\| null\fR
